 by a hormone binding assay  sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  the results of immunohistochemical staining for progesterone receptor protein are for investigational use only  they must not be used for clinical purposes  added by  frederick carl koerner  m d  signed on  18 removed_month 94 at 09 51 gross description  received fresh in the frozen section lab   labeled remove_patient_name  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a removed_date x removed_date x 0 5cm breast tissue fragment with a localizing wire and accompanying x ray  the specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a stellate  tan  firm mass  measuring removed_date x removed_date x 0 6cm abutting the inked margin  a representative section of the mass is frozen as frozen section  1  and saved frozen  the remainder of the suspicious region is submitted in cassettes a through d  and what is left of the specimen is submitted in cassettes e and f  resident  darryl e  palmer toy  md     intra operative diagnosis     frozen section diagnosis  1   left breast   infiltrating carcinoma  o r  resident  fang fang  md o r  diagnosis by  judith ann ferry  m d                                                                                  source care unit  surgical day care   acc 3 reports to  edwin lee carter  m d  part   left breast   report_end  , No.
