rs that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  when we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   in this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  the results of immunohistochemical staining for progesterone receptor protein are for investigational use only  they must not be used for clinical purposes  added by  frederick carl koerner  m d  signed on  02 removed_month 95 at 10 43 gross description  received fresh in the frozen section lab   labeled remove_patient_name  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast mass   is a removed_date x removed_date x 0 9cm fragment of breast tissue with localizing wire in place  inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable breast parenchyma  submitted entirely in cassettes a through i  gross description by  keith kwan  md resident  chin lee wu  md  phd     intra operative diagnosis     gross diagnosis  breast  right   no gross evidence of invasive carcinoma  o r  resident  edi brogi  md  phd o r  diagnosis by  eugene jerome mark  m d                                                                                  source care unit  same day surgical unit    removed_accession_id  reports to  edwin lee carter  m d  chin lee wu  m d  part   right breast biopsy , No.
